This directory should contain backup_public_key.asc - the GPG public key
that backup.yml encrypts every backup to. It's gitignored (see
ansible/.gitignore) since it's generated per-deployment, not shared across
clones of this repo - this file is the one that stays tracked in its place
so the directory isn't just silently empty.

To generate yours:

    gpg --export --armor <your-key-id-or-email> > files/backup_public_key.asc

Then set gpg_recipient_key_id in group_vars/all.yml to that same
id/email/fingerprint. Full context: docs/install.md ("2d. Set up the backup
encryption key") and docs/backup.md.

Keep the matching PRIVATE key only on your control machine (or wherever you
run restores from) - it must never be copied to the VPS. See docs/restore.md.
